WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.770
Sometimes, a movie's production just goes
so off the rails that the most humane thing

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.680
the filmmakers can do is to pull the plug.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:13.140
These are some previously-announced and greatly-anticipated
movies that reached the end of the line in

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:13.640
2019.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:18.980
Over the course of nearly 20 years, the X-Men
movie franchise placed its ensemble cast of

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:22.180
mutants in different points across various
timelines.

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:26.130
Wolverine was the first character to spin
off into his own sub-franchise, with X-Men

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:29.230
Origins: Wolverine, The Wolverine, and Logan.

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:33.520
For years, Fox tried to get more standalone
mutant movies off the ground, starting with

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:38.390
a proposed Origins follow-up focusing on Magneto,
though this project was eventually reworked

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:40.880
into the ensemble prequel X-Men: First Class.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:46.460
The other solo X-movie that's come close to
being a reality is one about Remy LeBeau,

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:52.489
a.k.a. Gambit, the Louisiana-born, staff-wielding
mutant who's notably adept at throwing explosive

00:00:52.489 --> 00:00:52.980
playing cards.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:58.620
Gambit is a fan favorite, having been a main
character on the '90s Saturday morning X-Men

00:00:58.620 --> 00:00:59.120
cartoon.

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:02.240
He even made a brief appearance in X-Men Origins:
Wolverine.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:05.140
"Are you Remy LeBeau?"

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:08.880
"Do I owe you money?"

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:09.980
"No."

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:13.060
"Then Remy LeBeau I am."

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:20.640
Fox stacked the deck for the film's chances
by casting likable, bankable Channing Tatum

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:21.160
in the title role.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:26.620
But the studio just couldn't get this movie
into play thanks to a seemingly never-ending

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.020
search for the right director to helm it.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:32.890
Gambit had been shuffled around a couple of
2019 release dates, but the ongoing director

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:34.740
search left its viability in question.

00:01:35.689 --> 00:01:40.920
As 2019 began, Fox had Gambit scheduled for
release in March 2020, despite not having

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.320
a director actively attached.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:48.060
Then Disney acquired Fox, throwing the smaller
studio's whole slate of projects into disarray.

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:53.400
In May 2019, the new bosses moved around the
release dates for a bunch of movies, including

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:53.900
Gambit.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:59.500
The Tatum vehicle went from a March 2020 release
to… currently nothing, disappearing from

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:00.000
the schedule.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:05.060
The enduring Star Trek big-screen franchise
flew high for decades.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:09.640
After focusing on the characters from the
original 1960s TV series, the movies shifted

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:14.060
focus to the world of Star Trek: The Next
Generation, ultimately sputtering out when

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:19.780
the 2002 entry Star Trek: Nemesis grossed
$43 million, the worst-ever showing for a

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:20.280
Trek movie.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:25.470
It took the visionary sci-fi mind of J.J.
Abrams to revive Star Trek movies for a new

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:30.420
generation, reviving well-known, old-school
characters like Kirk and Spock to create three

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:36.720
fun and contemporary blockbusters: Star Trek,
Star Trek Into Darkness, and Star Trek Beyond.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:43.020
That last one earned $158 million in the summer
of 2016, enough to merit a fourth entry.

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:47.210
Paramount announced the project at CinemaCon
2018, with S.J.

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:48.280
Clarkson attached to direct.

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:53.820
Zachary Quinto was reportedly up to reprise
his role as Spock, and Chris Hemsworth may

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:58.420
have returned, too, having played Captain
Kirk's father George in 2009's Star Trek.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:03.860
Not immediately on board, however, was Chris
Pine, the guy that plays the fairly important

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:04.580
role of Captain Kirk.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:09.680
Pine and Paramount couldn't come to an agreement
on a contract, and the same issue occurred

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:10.940
when trying to sign Hemsworth.

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:13.600
The studio ultimately canceled the entire
movie.

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:19.660
Amidst the 21st-century zombie craze that
gave us The Walking Dead and Pride and Prejudice

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:21.760
and Zombies came World War Z.

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:27.420
Based on the novel by Max Brooks, the movie
starred Brad Pitt as a globe-trekking, military-aligned

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:31.950
hero trying to stop the zombie hordes running
all over the world with their insatiable lust

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:32.440
for flesh.

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:38.760
The film ended with a hopeful-ish ending,
and it grossed a whopping $202 million at

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.840
the North American box office, ensuring a
sequel.

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:46.920
World War Z 2 seemed more promising than other
unnecessary sequels, if only because Seven

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:50.730
and Fight Club director David Fincher was
reportedly on board to direct.

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:55.620
There were vague rumors of a 2019 release
date, and according to The Playlist, Paramount

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:59.780
did everything it could to get the ball rolling
— but it never officially gave the thing

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:00.280
the green light.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:06.400
Everything fell apart, and as of February
2019, World War Z had crawled back into the

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:06.900
grave.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:12.160
Sequels and prequels are common movie conceits
— but crossover movies?

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:13.280
Not so much.

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:18.780
The most prominent modern mash-up of two established
properties on the big screen is probably Alien

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:19.829
vs. Predator.

00:04:19.829 --> 00:04:23.930
Sony hoped to pull off a face-off of its own
with two of its hit comedy brands, Men in

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:25.020
Black and Jump Street.

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:29.280
News of this proposed film hit the streets
via the 2014 Sony hack.

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:35.820
In one leaked document, studio co-chair Amy
Pascal floated the idea, and in an email,

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:39.500
Jump Street's Jonah Hill called the idea,
quote, "clean and rad and powerful."

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:44.820
Sony continued to develop the idea, and at
CinemaCon 2016 announced that the film would

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:48.820
be titled MIB 23, and that James Bobin would
direct.

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:53.060
But just a few months later, Hill seemed to
find the project neither rad nor powerful.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:54.660
He told the Toronto Sun:

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:56.800
"I doubt that movie will get made.

00:04:57.140 --> 00:05:01.419
The Jump Street films were so fun to make
and the whole joke of them was they were making

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:06.120
fun of remakes and sequels and reboots and
then now it's become a giant sequel, reboot."

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:12.379
In January 2019, MIB producer Walter Parkes
admitted it was all over, telling Empire,

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:13.849
quote, "We gave it a shot."

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:19.200
He went on to explain that the whole thing
turned out to be a, quote, "impossible match-up."

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:24.080
While Disney-owned Marvel proceeded full steam
ahead with its Marvel Cinematic Universe,

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:27.990
Sony remained determined to hold on to their
movie rights to Spider-Man.

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:33.499
The MCU solo Spidey stories starring Tom Holland
are co-productions between Sony and Marvel,

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:38.120
but Sony has also been focusing on spin-offs
centered primarily around offshoot characters

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:40.699
in Spider-Man's corner of the Marvel Universe.

00:05:40.699 --> 00:05:45.860
Among those films are the Oscar-winning animated
feature Into the Spider-Verse, the hit Venom

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:51.069
starring Tom Hardy, and the upcoming Morbius
— with Jared Leto portraying the "Living

00:05:51.069 --> 00:05:53.009
Vampire" — whatever the heck that is.

00:05:53.009 --> 00:05:56.319
There was also a proposed endeavor called
Silver &amp; Black.

00:05:56.319 --> 00:06:01.229
That film would showcase the adventures of
not one but two Spider-Man side characters:

00:06:01.229 --> 00:06:05.759
mercenary Silver Sable and cat burglar Black
Cat.

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:09.180
"You look good.

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:10.140
Been working out?"

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:11.260
"No.

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:13.720
I mean — you know, a little…"

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:20.860
In May 2017, Sony signed up Gina Prince-Bythewood
to direct, and charged ahead for a February

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:21.780
2019 release date.

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:27.220
That changed in June 2018, when the studio
altered its theatrical debut date to… no

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:28.620
date at all.

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:33.050
There had been a few problems along the way,
primarily that shooting hadn't yet begun.

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:36.700
One of the main problems, reportedly, was
that the director didn't like the shooting

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:37.200
script.

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:43.199
No screenplay and no release date usually
imply a movie is dead, but that's not exactly

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:43.780
the case here.

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:48.830
Shortly after Silver &amp; Black lost its street
date, Sony announced that it would instead

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:51.760
make two separate movies: one Silver, one
Black.

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:53.840
Hey — the more the merrier, right?

